{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/929304-staff-merit-and-extended-action","id":929304,"title":"Staff Merit and Extended Action","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T11:52:12-07:00","id":929304,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Staff Merit and Extended Action","content":"The Staff Merit provides one automatic success to a specified skill and CoFD rulebook says theyre not good for extended actions. RAI makes it seem like the merit is meant to work only by itself outside of he character. At the same time, it doesn't say anywhere that the merit cannot be used in tandem with a character's own dicepool.<br /> <br /> Would it be a terrible idea if I allow my players to use this merit in their own rolls both as a way to ensure at least one success in a normal roll and as a way to ensure they never fail a roll in an extended action?<br /> <br /> I can see how this might be flavourful and alright in-fiction, with a character as the head of a project who knows how to properly delegate basic and routine tasks. The merit in this case represents that the staff is not just any hired people to help them (that would be handled by Services) but a well put togeher team with members that trust each other and work well together.<br /> <br /> Example 1: A character who is a designer / engineer and has her own company with a trusted and tried team of programmers (Computer), engineers (Crafts) and designers (Expression) and works with them on a great project.<br /> <br /> Example 2: A cutthroat politician who intimately knows that the way to power requires good backing. He has at his disposal a team responsible for fundraising events (Socialize), PR-consultants (Expression) and lobbyists (Persuasion) ready to support him in all steps to win the senatorial election.<br /> <br /> Example 3: A commander of men and armies has at her disposal a good staff for intelligence analysis (Investigation), forward observers for artillery and air strikes (Firearms) and drone controllers (Computer) who helps the commander every step on the way to defeat the enemy.<br /> <br /> Also, in this way the merit would work well together with other social merits.<br /> <br /> Example 4: don Luca, head of the city underworld, needs to expand into thus far unknown areas in the city. He makes sure to cash in on a favour owed by local smugglers (Allies: smugglers) to know who's who and what's what in this place. The merit for these smuggler allies is worth 2 dots, while the sevice itself is a level 3 which means don Luca would strain his relationship with them, luckily his staff of information gatherers (Streetwise) can do a portion of the job and thus the favour asked of the smugglers is not too great. don Luca finds that many businesses in this area actually are under the protection of the Jigarow family. He sends out his trusted Retainer don John to &quot;persuade&quot; them of his own, more benificial, terms and allows a gang of thugs (Intimidation) accompany him, just to be sure. A war is bound to break out with the Jigarows and don Luca needs to have the local authorities and politicians on his side. He looks over his Contacts (politicians) to find out who to pay a visit, getting useful help from his experts on political matters (Politics) and instantly knows where to go next...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 07-10-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:27:24-07:00","id":929326,"title":"","content":"The rules say they aren't useful in contested actions. Which is true, since contested actions compared successes. A staff that provides 1 success to perception rolls for security might stop inept shoplifters, but is a minor speed bump to any sort of thievery focused character.<br /> <br /> It makes no comment on extended actions.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, it would be a terrible idea for them to be able to apply 1 success per appropriate staff member to the player's rolls, extended or not. 5 Merit dots for potentially +5 successes per roll is insanely powerful.<br /> <br /> Just use the basic teamwork rules, esp. as it slots in very neatly: any appropriate staff member can perform a support teamwork action to the player's roll. Since they automatically generate 1 success, this translates into +1 dice for the player to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:51:02-07:00","id":929340,"title":"","content":"Thank you for correcting me, Heavy Arms, the book says they are not useful in CONTESTED actions.<br /> And your idea of letting them net a +1 bonus die is a neat one.<br /> <br /> That said, it seems like you missinterpret the Staff merit. The merit can never add more than 1 success per roll, if I read the description correctly. You need the Mentor merit to have more than 1 success on a given roll.<br /> <br /> CoFD rulebook, page 54:<br /> &quot;For every dot in this Merit, choose one type of assistant, and one Skill. At any reasonable time, his staff can take actions using that Skill. These actions automatically garner a single success. While not useful in contested actions, this guarantees success on minor, mundane activities. Note that your character may have employees without requiring the Staff Merit; Staff simply adds a mechanical advantage for those groups.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, yes, a 5-dot Staff provides 5 successes, but only one success each to five distinct rolls with different skills.<br /> <br /> I bring up this subject because I want to explore the reasons to even have this merit instead of Retainer, or frankly most other social merits. Allowing this seems to make it fill a mechanical and in-fiction niche that the others don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 07-10-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:25:19-07:00","id":929410,"title":"","content":"The Merit never specifies that each staff member has to have a different Skill type. There's nothing stopping my character that runs a video game company from having Staff 5 and them all be programmers with Computers as their Skill. If you let them add their successes to my characters actions as their action instead of getting 1 success on their grunt work programming stuff, what stops them from all adding together for +5?<br /> <br /> The reason to take this is that you get numbers and reliability without any real drawbacks. Mentors want stuff from you (and they don't directly boost your rolls either). Retainers have a lot more individual potential, but Staff 5 is generally better than five one dot Retainers (since the Staff are five NPCs that get 1 automatic success per action, and the Retainers are stuff to 2 dice in their good rolls), even if the Retainers are a bit more flexible; Retainers also want more than a steady paycheck. Allies, Status, and Resources all have limits on how much aid you can call on. Contacts doesn't really invoke direct dice bonuses. Etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:45:05-07:00","id":929452,"title":"","content":"Alright, I see your point. I simply assumed, RAI, a merit would not give 5 successes to a Skill since that would be pretty brutal. One could cheaply substitute loads of Skills, especially mental ones, with this merit without any real drawback if you are correct (provided, of course, if the ST allows it). Also, would not such an interpretation somewhat challenge the idea of it not being useful in contested action? Not many characters, or average NPCs for that matter, could continuously produce 5 successes on every roll.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your input though: I am likely to take what you say into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}